new('plaints','plaindre','past participle masculine plural','pitied; felt compassion for',['blamed','envied','forgotten'],'Il a éprouvé de la compassion pour eux : il les a ___.',['plaints','blâmés','enviés','oubliés'],'Quel participe pluriel signifie considérés avec compassion ?','sns_cendrillon_plaindre_prendre_en_pitie_les_maux_d_autrui_en_etre_touche_temoigner_la_compassion_que_l_on_eprouve_pour_quelqu_un_3ef7087cc8',note='After les avoir plaints the dwarf pities their apparent weakness; this is transitive pity, not reflexive complain. The published compassion sense and earlier complaining plan were compared. Plural participial agreement follows les, while the same pity meaning remains shared.')
new('demanda','demander','verb past historic singular information','asked; sought to know',['refused','hid','forgot'],'Il posa une question pour obtenir cette information : il ___ s’ils étaient heureux.',['demanda','ignora','cacha','oublia'],'Quel verbe au passé simple signifie posa une question pour savoir ?','sns_zola_demander_ask',note='The indirect questions ask about their past, activities, happiness, reproduction and soul. The existing exact candidate bank asks for an object/permission; the global family also has the distinct ask-information sense. Link that sense with its own demanda bank, without confusing asking questions with demanding a thing.')
new('été','être','past participle spatial presence','been; been situated',['slept','sung','worked'],'Dans cette hypothèse, sa tête aurait ___ au-dessus des nuages, c’est-à-dire située plus haut qu’eux.',['été','dormi','chanté','travaillé'],'Quel participe indique ici qu’une chose se serait trouvée dans un lieu ?','sns_fr_etre_presence',occ=[(160,111)],note='Sa tête eût été au-dessus locates the head spatially in the counterfactual. The other été use describes their misérable état and retains the copular identity; the passive and summer banks are excluded. Use the published presence sense for this participial form, preserving earlier spatial été dependency reconciliation.')
new('misérable','misérable','adjective singular pitiable','wretched; pitiable',['fortunate','splendid','comfortable'],'Cet état inspire la pitié tant il paraît malheureux : il est ___.',['misérable','heureux','splendide','confortable'],'Quel adjectif qualifie un état qui inspire la pitié ?','sns_parure_miserable_qui_est_reduit_a_la_misere_qui_inspire_la_pitie_d069b3e0e8',note='The dwarf pities the humans’ tiny condition close to nonexistence. The global family includes reduced-to-misery/pity as well as a meagre monetary-value sense. Pitiable condition uses the former; new questions avoid limiting the source to poverty or an inadequate salary.')
